      <Desc>Outreach DevelopmentOur core dance and teaching artists work year round, teaching dance classes (for dancers and non-dancers alike) offered by donation to the public, and developing performances and collaborations throughout San Diego. These artists are committed to education and art practice that lead by example, and uphold the mission of our organization, to move dance towards community, justice, and radical expression.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>28824</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>12708</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Queer Mvmnt FestThrough an intersectional lens, Queer Mvmnt Fest, has highlighted LGBTQ+ artists with emphasis on BIPOC contributors, through performance, workshops, discussions, and classes for affinity groups and the general public. These funds were used to pay contracted artists and the resources to support them such as rehearsal and performance space, and administrative and production staff.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
